[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ## Materialization (Online → Offline)
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For online FGs (`online_enabled=True, stream=True`), data written to Kafka/RonDB must be materialized to the offline store (Delta Lake) via a Spark job.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ### Do NOT Start Materialization on Every Insert
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] If you are doing multiple inserts (e.g., batch pipeline, multi-part insert, iterative processing), **do not trigger a materialization job after each insert**. Each materialization launches a Spark job which consumes cluster resources. Instead:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Pattern: Materialize once after all inserts complete:**
[agent:result] ```python
[agent:result] # Do all inserts first
[agent:result] fg.insert(batch_1, wait=False)
[agent:result] fg.insert(batch_2, wait=False)
[agent:result] fg.insert(batch_3, wait=False)
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Then materialize once
[agent:result] fg.materialization_job.run(await_termination=True)
[agent:result] ```
